### Architecture Notes
Existing pattern: skill-enabled agents declare a `skills:` block list, while `src/owlbear/core/agent_registry.py` appends the shared `SkillRegistry` whenever `defn.skills` is non-empty. This task changes agent metadata and test expectations only; it does not introduce a new runtime mechanism.

The original task description missed two stale assertions in `tests/test_pipeline_e2e.py` that still encoded `researcher.skills == []`. Those assertions are part of the same contract surface and had to be pulled into scope or the builder would inherit an avoidable failing-test gap.

This remains one domain: agent-definition configuration. Adding `kanban` or `terminal` tools to researcher or curator would be a separate capability-change task.

### Changes Made
- Rewrote the task body into six verifiable acceptance criteria.
- Expanded the affected file list to include `tests/test_pipeline_e2e.py`.
- Preserved the out-of-scope boundary that direct kanban and terminal execution are not part of this task.
- Appended architecture notes for the builder and reviewer.

### Dependencies
- Added/Removed/Verified: no explicit task dependencies; verified existing skill wiring in `src/owlbear/core/agent_registry.py`; verified existing skill-list pattern in `src/owlbear/agents/builder.md` and `src/owlbear/agents/auditor.md`.